-- ownership: a summary as wide as its result's type (`ownership-checker.md`
-- §16.7, amended 2026-10-16). `w8` places its argument at 256 result paths,
-- which the tuple type it returns bounds, and its summary names every one
-- of them: no path is cut to fit a cap. So the caller sees exactly that the
-- result holds the argument at `.0.0.0.0.0.0.0.0`, and extending that list
-- while the argument is read later is rejected `alias`, exact. Under the old
-- cap of 64 paths the summary was coarsened and the same edit was rejected
-- `call`, approximate.
w1 x = ( x, x )


w2 x = w1 (w1 x)


w4 x = w2 (w2 x)


w8 x = w4 (w4 x)


pub wide : List Int → Int
wide xs =
    t = w8 xs
    ys = [ …t.0.0.0.0.0.0.0.0, 1 ]
    List.length ys + List.length xs
